Checkout/push SDK and native dependencies
-----------------------------------------

cade-git uses git2 for existing-worktree checkout and feature-specific push
upload. Gitoxide (gix) retains local operations, clone/fetch, push validation
and fresh remote observation. git2 is pinned to 0.21.0 with default features
disabled and https plus vendored-libgit2 enabled; cade-github also uses this
workspace dependency for Host-owned push transport construction. SSH is not
enabled. The fallback does not replace gix.

The checkout-added Cargo.lock packages and their installed source notices are:

- git2 0.21.0 and libgit2-sys 0.18.8+1.9.7, from rust-lang/git2-rs:
  Cargo.toml declares MIT OR Apache-2.0. See each package's LICENSE-MIT
  and LICENSE-APACHE. Both LICENSE-MIT files state:
  Copyright (c) 2014 Alex Crichton
- libz-sys 1.1.30, from rust-lang/libz-sys:
  Cargo.toml declares MIT OR Apache-2.0. See LICENSE-MIT and
  LICENSE-APACHE. LICENSE-MIT states:
  Copyright (c) 2014 Alex Crichton
  Copyright (c) 2020 Josh Triplett

The Rust binding licenses do not replace the native library licenses.
The historical macOS checkout build compiled vendored libgit2 1.9.7 and
linked it statically. The #600 manifest now explicitly selects the bundled
library, and the October 27, 2026 batch16 Darwin build receipt also records
static libgit2 with HTTPS/vendor features. This is native build evidence,
not native HTTPS acceptance. Its source is included in libgit2-sys under libgit2/:

  libgit2 is Copyright (C) the libgit2 contributors,
  unless otherwise stated. See the AUTHORS file for details.

libgit2/COPYING supplies GNU GPL version 2 with a linking exception and
separate notices for bundled components. The installed build.rs selects
bundled llhttp (MIT), xdiff (LGPL-2.1-or-later, per deps/xdiff/xdiff.h),
PCRE2 (PCRE2 Licence, including its BSD terms) and SHA1 collision detection
(MIT). Without HTTPS, the earlier checkout build selected built-in RFC 6234
SHA256 code (the IETF Trust notice in COPYING). With HTTPS, build.rs instead
selects CommonCrypto SHA256 on Apple targets, OpenSSL SHA256 on non-Apple
Unix targets, and Win32 SHA256 on Windows. Retained source notices are not
a claim that every bundled source component is linked into every build.
For their full terms and other component-specific notices, retain the
upstream COPYING and source notices; do not treat every bundled file as
covered only by the Rust bindings' MIT OR Apache-2.0 declaration.
The bundled wildmatch acknowledgment in COPYING is:
This product includes software developed by Rich Salz.

libz-sys supplies the zlib binding; the captured macOS build links system
zlib (-lz), not a newly built bundled zlib archive. The installed
libz-sys source also carries stock zlib under src/zlib/; its LICENSE is
the zlib license and states:
 (C) 1995-2026 Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler
This source notice does not identify the version of the system library
linked on a particular machine.

The captured native link output also names macOS iconv, Security and
CoreFoundation. These build observations are not an inventory of shipped
installers or a guarantee of other platforms' native linkage.
This attribution inventory is not a substitute for upstream license texts,
an exhaustive distribution review, or legal/release certification.

Clone/fetch feature dependencies
-------------------------------

cade-git clone/fetch and cade-github's Git connection use the existing
gix 0.90.0 SDK with blocking-http-transport-reqwest-native-tls and
worktree-mutation enabled. This feature change preserves existing resolved
package versions; clone/fetch do not use git2 transport. The separate #600
push HTTPS feature addition is described below; SSH remains disabled.

The ten added Cargo.lock packages are listed below. License declarations
and notice filenames were read from their installed registry sources:

- crossbeam 0.8.5 and crossbeam-queue 0.3.14:
  MIT OR Apache-2.0; LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE in each package.
  Copyright (c) 2019 The Crossbeam Project Developers
- dua-core 4.2.0, from Byron/dua-cli:
  Cargo.toml declares MIT. The installed package contains no LICENSE file;
  this metadata declaration is not a claim that its full notice was bundled
  or that a distribution review is complete.
- gix-credentials 0.42.1, gix-negotiate 0.38.0, gix-prompt 0.19.1 and
